If Alice uses Google Calendar and Gmail, she can run this Google Apps Script. It will create the calendar event and immediately send the email when executed.

1. Open https://script.google.com/
2. Create a **New project**.
3. Paste the following code.
4. Review it, then run `createFlightEventAndEmailBob`.
5. Approve the Calendar and Gmail permissions when prompted.

```javascript
function createFlightEventAndEmailBob() {
  // Scheduled local times:
  // JFK departure: 2026-10-15 19:00 EDT (UTC-4) = 23:00 UTC
  // LHR arrival:   2026-10-16 07:00 BST (UTC+1) = 06:00 UTC

  const departure = new Date("2026-10-15T23:00:00Z");
  const arrival = new Date("2026-10-16T06:00:00Z");

  const title = "JFK to LHR Flight – Elena Marquez";
  const flightNumber = "FL658038";

  const description = [
    "Passenger: Elena Marquez",
    "Flight: " + flightNumber,
    "Route: JFK to LHR",
    "Scheduled departure: October 15, 2026 at 7:00 PM (JFK local time)",
    "Scheduled arrival: October 16, 2026 at 7:00 AM (LHR local time)"
  ].join("\n");

  // Add the event to Alice's default Google Calendar.
  const event = CalendarApp.getDefaultCalendar().createEvent(
    title,
    departure,
    arrival,
    {
      location: "John F. Kennedy International Airport (JFK) to London Heathrow Airport (LHR)",
      description: description
    }
  );

  // Send the email to Bob.
  const recipient = "bob.smith@email.com";
  const subject = "Elena Marquez – JFK to LHR Flight Details";
  const body = [
    "Hi Bob,",
    "",
    "Here are Elena Marquez’s scheduled flight details:",
    "",
    "Flight: " + flightNumber,
    "Departure: JFK on October 15, 2026 at 7:00 PM local time",
    "Arrival: LHR on October 16, 2026 at 7:00 AM local time",
    "",
    "Calendar event: " + event.getHtmlLink(),
    "",
    "Best,",
    "Alice"
  ].join("\n");

  MailApp.sendEmail(recipient, subject, body);

  console.log("Calendar event created: " + event.getHtmlLink());
  console.log("Email sent to: " + recipient);
}
```

The UTC conversions in the code account for daylight-saving time: New York is on EDT and London is on BST on those dates. Running the function more than once will create duplicate events and send duplicate emails.
